    "description": "Coriolis gas meter, manufacturers mark Micro Motion. The HPC020 High Pressure Coriolis Meter is used with a 5700 transmitter. The measurement sensor consists of a housing in which two parallel measuring tubes are mounted with one drive coil and two pick-off coils; processing of the measurement signals is performed by the same external device that controls the drive coil, and the natural frequency of the tubes is used to determine the gas density. The 5700 transmitter either uses an integral core processor (direct connection to the flow sensor) or is connected to an external core processor. Transmitter hardware and sealing procedure are documented in folder no. TC8519. Installation: measurement sensor and 5700 transmitter must be electronically sealed; programmable parameters: security mode settings, low flow cut off settings, damping settings, slug flow settings, last measured value fault timeout settings. Operation: horizontal flow direction only, no reverse flow during custody transfer; no pressure, temperature or density correction allowed during custody transfer. Verification: zero flow calibration per procedure C-SP-HW-280 for custody transfer in gas applications; one full calibration curve according to OIML R137-1&2:2012 for gas density >= 3.8 kg/m3; calibration with gas similar to the process gas at an ISO17025 lab or with a reference installation traceable to (inter)national standards."
